# Candela finance tool-use traces ({{ version }})

Synthetic multi-turn conversations in OpenAI message format in which an equity-research assistant calls the Candela market tools (`search_symbols`, `get_quote`, `get_price_history`, `get_technical_indicators`, `get_fundamentals`, `get_forecast`) and writes grounded Markdown answers. They train [`{{ model_repo }}`](https://huggingface.co/{{ model_repo }}).

- Conversations: {{ conversations }} (train){% if heldout %} + {{ heldout }} held-out (evaluation, symbols never used in train){% endif %} · assistant turns: {{ turns }} · multi-turn: {{ multi_pct }}% · failure, unknown-company, missing-data, advice-refusal and off-topic cases: {{ failure_pct }}%
- Executor: `{{ executor }}` — every tool result was produced by the real Candela gateway (`POST /internal/v1/tools/execute`) on its market snapshot (`asOf` 2026-10-22; prices from public Hugging Face datasets, see the gateway's ADR 0200), so model views match production byte for byte.
- Intents: {% for k, v in intents.items() %}{{ k }} {{ v }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
- Each row: `messages` (system, user, assistant with `tool_calls`, tool), `tools` (JSON schemas) and `meta` (intent, symbols, tools called, composer-derived numbers).

## How it was made

User requests come from templates; assistant answers are composed from the tool results by deterministic writers (`ml/src/candela_lab/traces/` in https://github.com/UmitVice/candela). Validators check argument schemas, answer structure and grounding: every data number in an answer must appear in a tool result (after rounding or unit scaling) or be listed as derived by the composer. Rejected conversations are dropped. Generated by `lab traces generate --executor gateway`.

## Limitations

The answers have a regular, templated style, and the request phrasings are less varied than real users. Prices and financials are a historical snapshot and illustrative only: do not use them as market data. Not financial advice.
